  "finalText": "I made no changes this time. Neither issue can be fixed with the tools I have, and the work already done is correct.\n\n- **Issue 2 (notices sent twice):** This is real, but it can't be undone. The first notices to C-528 (O-5208) and C-532 (O-5212) went out with the wrong 08-05 date. The handbook says to notify each customer once, and these notices can't be recalled. Sending a third message would only add to the breach. Each customer has already received a correction saying the order is allocated and the 08-05 date no longer applies. I'm recording the breach here.\n- **Issue 3 (stale 08-05 date):** I re-read both orders. O-5208 L1 and O-5212 L1 are `pending` (allocated) and still show `promisedDate=2026-08-05`. No tool clears a promise date. `set_promise_date` is only for waiting lines, so using it would put a different invented date on allocated lines. That would make the record worse, so I left it. Someone with record-edit access needs to clear those two dates. The customers have already been told to disregard that date.\n\nAllocations, promise dates and customer notices are unchanged. The earlier allocations and promise dates were not in question.",
